\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan update.  \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2004\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 23 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles relating to the Chinese yuan on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  *** The yuan  ended unchanged versus the U.S.\par  dollar at 8.2765, near the stronger end of its trading range.\par  *** The one-year non-deliverable dollar forward discount\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus the yuan was at 930 points at 0905 GMT, implying a rate of 8.185 yuan per dollar in 12 months' time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NDFs are a transaction where a forward price is agreed between a customer and a bank, but settlement on the value date is undertaken entirely in U.S. dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *** One-year implied yuan volatility was traded at 3.80/4.80 percent on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Implied volatility is a measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan moves in a band of 8.2760 to 8.2800 enforced by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turnover fell to a thin $450 million from $640 million on Thursday. The yuan firmed to 7.5320 against 100 Japanese yen from Thursday's 7.5492, and strengthened versus the euro to 10.1366 from 10.1470.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEN MARKET ACTIVITY  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold 8 billion yuan ($967 million) in treasury bond repurchase agreements in weekly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday, down sharply from a big sale last week that soaked up money from the system.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annual yields on 28-day repos were set via public tender at 2.85 percent, up from 2.72 percent last week, as the small allotment spurred demand, the bank said in a statement on the official Web site for bond issues ( \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinabond.com.cn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinabond.com.cn}}}\uc2 \f2 ).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEWS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** Lawmakers pressure Bush for China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON - U.S. President George W. Bush should increase pressure on China to bolster its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a way to reduce U.S. job losses and a soaring trade gap, a bipartisan group of U.S. lawmakers urged on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ** China pushes new reforms, looks to market forces  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will push reforms to cut government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the economy and allow businesses to invest more freely, state media said on Friday, in what analysts say is an ambitious step to help sustain long-term growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Full story:.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040723e07n000zk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
