\par\par \b \uc2 China to expand  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market to help reform yuan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2004\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, June 9 (Reuters) - China plans to expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by allowing new instruments and more firms to trade to help improve the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said on Wednesday  \par \par \uc2 China would "further develop and improve the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and perfect the formation mechanism of the renminbi (yuan) exchange rate", the State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE) said in a statement on its Web site:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.safe.gov.cn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.safe.gov.cn}}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 SAFE would "actively expand forward business in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying and selling and study plans to increase the entities and products on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market", it said.  \par \par \uc2 The statement followed the signing of a memorandum of understanding between the Chicago Mercantile Exchange and China's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading System - to develop \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives in China.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. futures exchange said on Tuesday it would provide advice and expertise in the development of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives for China.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said the pact was part of "establishing the right financial architecture" before China could move to a flexible exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 Currently, the official \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is tightly controlled with commercial banks conducting almost all trades and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the top player, keeping the yuan stable through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 U.S. officials have been pressing \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revalue the yuan , which is pegged at about 8.28 to the dollar, amid criticism that the artificially cheap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is helping Chinese exports at the cost of U.S. manufacturing jobs.  \par \par \uc2 China has resisted such pressure, saying it will make the yuan more flexible by introducing reforms in its own time. But speculation has risen that China could shift to a system under which the yuan it tied to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Chinese officials have pledged to take steps to let market forces play a bigger role in determining the yuan's value and pave the way for its full convertibility.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have outlined steps to shore up the market, including allowing banks to become "market makers" and letting firms participate in the market. ($1=8.277 Yuan).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040609e069000sg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
