\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan update - March 9.  \b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 9 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles relating to the Chinese yuan on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  MARKETS   \par \par \uc2  *** The yuan  ended one notch firmer versus the U.S. dollar at 8.2771, remaining near the stronger end of its managed trading range.   \par \par \uc2  *** The one-year non-deliverable dollar forward discount versus the yuan  was at 3,800 points at 0820 GMT, implying a rate of 7.898 yuan per dollar in 12 months' time.   \par \par \uc2  NDFs are transactions where a forward price is agreed between a customer and a bank, but settlement on the value date is undertaken entirely in U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2  *** One-year implied yuan volatility  was traded at 7.60/7.90 percent on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility is a measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option.   \par \par \uc2  The yuan moves in a band of 8.2760 to 8.2800 enforced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Turnover was not immediately available on Tuesday. It fell to $490 million on Monday. The yuan weakened to 7.4330 against 100 Japanese yen from 7.3811, and softened against the euro to 10.2930 from 10.2360.   \par \par \uc2  OPEN MARKET ACTIVITY   \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China issued a hefty 60 billion yuan ($7.25 billion) in short-term commercial bills in weekly open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, 10 billion yuan more than last week. It is the largest batch issued since August 19 2003.   \par \par \uc2  NEWS   \par \par \uc2  **China \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill yields fall amid flush money   \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI - Yields of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  short-term bills fell after weekly open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, hit by an abundance of funds in the market.   \par \par \uc2  Full story:   \par \par \uc2  **Snow says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  no way to strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON - U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said on Monday that China was definitely moving toward a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate and warned that no country could maintain a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Full story:   \par \par \uc2  **US panel rejects latest \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  import curb request   \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON - The U.S. International Trade Commission rejected a request from American bed spring manufacturers on Monday for emergency protection against imports from China which it is felt have an unfair advantage due to the US$-pegged Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Full story:   \par \par \uc2  **China central banker - yuan to stay stable, growth at 7pct   \par \par \uc2  BASEL, Switzerland - China's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Li Ruogu said on Monday 7-8 pct economic growth this year is reasonable and there are no plans for monetary tightening in the world's sixth-biggest economy.   \par \par \uc2  Full story:   \par \par \uc2  **China warns of foreign debt amid yuan talk   \par \par \uc2  BEIJING - China's rising foreign debt, fuelled partly by speculation of a possible yuan revaluation, is creating economics risks, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief was quoted on Monday as saying.   \par \par \uc2  Full story:. 