\par\par \b \uc2 Daily Chinese yuan update - Jan 30.  \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2004\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 30 (Reuters) - Following is a summary of market activity and news articles relating to the Chinese yuan on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS  \par \par \uc2 *** The yuan ended three notches firmer versus the U.S. dollar at 8.2768, near the stronger end of its managed trading range.  \par \par \uc2 *** The one-year non-deliverable dollar forward discount versus the yuan was at 3,800 points at 0730 GMT, implying a rate of 7.898 yuan per dollar in 12 months' time.  \par \par \uc2 NDFs are transactions where a forward price is agreed between a customer and a bank, but settlement on the value date is undertaken entirely in U.S. dollars.  \par \par \uc2 *** One-year implied yuan volatility was traded at 8.00/10.00 percent on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Implied volatility is a measure of how much the options market expects the price of the underlying asset to move during the life of the option.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan moves in a band of 8.2760 to 8.2800 enforced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Turnover, a moderate $760 million on Thursday, was not immediately available. The yuan firmed to 7.8038 against 100 Japanese yen from 7.8132, and strengthened against the euro to 10.2689 from 10.3177.  \par \par \uc2 OPEN MARKET ACTIVITY  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued up to 10 billion yuan ($1.2 billion) in short-term commercial bills on January 21 in token open market action aimed at mopping up excess money supply, down from the previous week's 26 billion yuan.  \par \par \uc2 NEWS  \par \par \uc2 ** U.S. coalition pushes ahead on China \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  case  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON - A coalition of U.S. farm, labour and manufacturing groups took the first step on Thursday toward asking the Bush administration to investigate whether \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an unfair trade practice warranting U.S. retaliation.  \par \par \uc2 Full story:  \par \par \uc2 ** VW to invest fewer euros in China due to weak yuan  \par \par \uc2 ESSEN, Germany - Germany's Volkswagen AG (VOWG.DE) said on Thursday it would invest fewer euros in the booming Chinese auto market than it had originally earmarked because a weak Chinese yuan made the investment more valuable.  \par \par \uc2 Full story:  \par \par \uc2 ** Foreign central banks keep buying U.S. debt - Fed  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK - Holdings of U.S. debt by foreign central banks leaped again in the latest week to touch a record high, driven mainly by purchases of agency bonds.  \par \par \uc2 Full story:.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040130e01u00uyb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
