\par\par \b \uc2 UDPATE 2-US Treasury Sec Snow  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  hearing set for Oct 30.  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 23:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 14 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's Senate testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been delayed, has been rescheduled for Oct. 30, a Senate Banking Committee spokesman said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The committee expects to receive a Treasury report on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  - originally due Oct. 15 - in time for the hearing, committee spokesman Andrew Gray said.  \par \par \uc2 Snow's testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  was originally due to be given on Thursday but was delayed so the panel could hear from the Treasury secretary on regulation of U.S. mortgage finance markets.  \par \par \uc2 "Regulatory reform of the (government-sponsored mortgage finance enterprises) is a legislative and scheduling priority," Gray said.  \par \par \uc2 A Treasury spokesman said the report, which exmaines whether major trading partners have manipulated their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain a trade advantage over the United States, would not be delivered to lawmakers until the day of the hearing.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturers have blamed weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad - particularly in China - for their competitive woes. President George W. Bush is expected to pressure Chinese and Japanese leaders on the issue when he travels to Asia later this week.  \par \par \uc2 China keeps the yuan pegged to the dollar, and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely but its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bush administration would like \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japanese authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less to weaken the yen against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturers, who have shed about 2.7 million jobs over three years, are a critical base of support for Bush in the run-up to next year's presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Last month, finance officials from the Group of Seven rich nations issued a statement calling for more flexibility in exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031014dzae002pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
