\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Higher Late; Shadow Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Cris Larano  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2003\par 12:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were higher late Friday, buoyed by exporters' dollar sales, but trading was generally lackluster as participants continued to await further direction from the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 A call made last weekend by the Group of Seven richest nations for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility continued to hold sway in the region, but few \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players were ready to take Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher amid a lingering view the Japanese authorities would sell yen to support the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Participants were also assessing the longer term impact of rising oil prices, after the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries this week decided to cut production, on Asian economies.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is just taking stock of recent movements we've seen across the board," said Peter Redward, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. "The G7 meeting has been a watershed for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets."  \par \par \uc2 "I think the market is just wondering what's going to happen, whether the Bank of Japan will come in or not," Redward added.  \par \par \uc2 Jimmy Koh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UOB in Singapore, said the trigger for the dollar's trend reversal against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a substantial fall in the Nikkei.  \par \par \uc2 Shares in the region weakened this week on worries over the potential dual impact of stronger Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 "If we see a few more days of a Nikkei sell-off, then it would be a self-correcting mechanism for the dollar," he said, referring to the possibility that the Bank of Japan could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the dollar if Japanese equity prices plummet.  \par \par \uc2 In South Korea, as elsewhere in the region, exporters took advantage of Thursday's dollar rise and unloaded their holdings of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The feeling is that exporters will continue to sell dollars on any gains as the longer term view is for a weaker dollar, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea was suspected of having bought dollars but the U.S. unit still closed lower at KRW1,150.5, down from KRW1,151.6 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Aggressive dollar sales by local exporters pressured the greenback and foreign net buying in the stock market also hammered the dollar," said a trader at Woori Bank.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, appears more effective in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the yuan ended weaker on suspected dollar buying by monetary authorities, while the one-year dollar-yuan nondeliverable forwards discount widened after tightening Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 In the offshore NDF market, the bid-and-offer quote for the one-year dollar-yuan NDF stood at a discount of 3300-3000 to the yuan in afternoon trading, wider than 2950-2750 late Thursday afternoon as the yuan revaluation speculation continued to affect market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 Redward believes the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  still have sufficient room to appreciate against the U.S. dollar since the rise in many regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not been as large as that of the yen and the euro.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Philippines, Hong Kong, Malaysia, India and China have actually depreciated in trade-weighted terms, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "In aggregate, Asia has actually experienced a modest fall in the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely because China hasn't moved and these five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have in effect depreciated," Redward added.  \par \par \uc2 In Taiwan, trade competitiveness played a role in the New Taiwan dollar's movement Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Taipei \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced in step with the yen to ensure the competitiveness of its technology exports against that of Japan. However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's retreat was tempered by banks covering short positions after Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it was closely monitoring global hot money flows.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at NT$33.791 Friday, down from NT$33.795.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar was higher late Friday, lifted by early gains in the yen and weak market sentiment for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in the wake of recent economic data such as August durable goods orders which continued to fuel doubts over the strength of the U.S.' economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 At 0805 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7315, down from S1.7338 in late Asian trading Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Meantime, banks paring their excess dollar holdings provided a boost to the Philippine peso. The dollar closed at PHP55.02, down from PHP55.15 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 In Indonesia, the rupiah was unchanged at IDR8,440 against the dollar, as month-end dollar demand from local importers offset the influence from a firmer yen.  \par \par \uc2 -By Chris Larano, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288; cris.larano@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lim Mui Khi  \par \par \uc2 1136 4250  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030926dz9q000gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
