\par\par \b \uc2  US Snow: It Is 'Critical' China Adopt Flexible  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Price \par \uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2003\par 17:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par    BEIJING -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. and China on Tuesday agreed to\par disagree on the pace with which China moves to a flexible exchange\par rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said he argued forcefully for China\par to ease capital restrictions and move expeditiously toward a\par market-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system in meetings Tuesday with China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Zhou Xiaochuan, Finance Minister Jin Renqing, and Vice\par Premier Huang Ju.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "We expressed our view it is in China's interest to have a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and to continue the process of reducing controls on capital flows in and out," Snow told reporters after the talks. "It is critical they move." \par \par \uc2  If China were to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate rigid, but relax capital flow restrictions, it would risk building "discontinuities" into the financial system, Snow said. He has long argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's practice of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 8.28 yuan per U.S. dollar deprives it of a safety valve for absorbing economic shocks. \par \par \uc2  But Chinese officials made clear in a statement earlier Tuesday that they have no intentions of adjusting the peg. \par \par \uc2  "We will maintain the current stable yuan policy," a spokesman for the People's Bank of China told Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  U.S. manufacturers have complained increasingly loudly about China's fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, which they say holds the yuan at artificially low levels and gives Chinese exporters unfair advantage. They have demanded Snow pressure the Chinese to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen to reflect mounting trade surpluses and investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  A senior U.S. Treasury official, speaking on conditions of anonymity, said the Chinese briefed Snow on steps either underway or due to be announced shortly that would in effect relax the capital controls. For example, on Monday, China recently announced it would raise the limit on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that can be purchased by residents traveling abroad to $5000 from $2000. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. official said Treasury viewed the visit, Snow's first to China as Treasury Secretary, as the start of a series of discussions on the issue. \par \par \uc2  Snow is meeting with senior leaders in China following talks in Tokyo, which also touched on the need for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility within the region. He will fly to Phuket, Thailand, late Wednesday to meet his regional counterparts at an annual Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation finance ministers' meeting. \par \par \uc2  -By Elizabeth Price, Dow Jones Newswires; 41 79 312 9472; Elizabeth.Price@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030902dz9200112\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
