\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Edges Marginally Higher Vs Dlr In Active Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2002\par 06:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan was marginally higher against the U.S. dollar Friday in active trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the dollar stood at 8.2767 yuan, down from 8.2768 Thursday, after trading in a narrow range of CNY8.2766 and CNY8.2768 throughout the session. \par \par \uc2  "Both dollar-buyers and sellers are active today," a Beijing-based trader at a state-owned commercial bank said. Trading volume is unavailable on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site. \par \par \uc2  Most of the deals were conducted at CNY8.2767 to the dollar, and the trader suspects that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supporting the dollar on a regular basis throughout the session to keep the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from slipping further. China's dollar supply remains high due to the healthy trade surplus. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the yuan's exchange rate in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was flat at CNY1.0608. The Japanese yen was lower at CNY 6.6084 per 100 yen from CNY6.6478, while the euro was weaker at CNY8.0448 from CNY8.0970 amid thin trading. \par \par \uc2  China tightly controls the flow of capital across its borders, allowing only partial convertibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the capital account. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on the current account is also tightly monitored and the value of the yuan is held in a narrow band against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021018dyai0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
