\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan climbs two ticks in active trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Oct 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened two ticks against the U.S. dollar to 8.2767 in active trade on Monday as exporters sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was a busy $640 million on Monday, although down from a heavy $740 million on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There were a lot of people selling today," said a dealer at a state-owned bank in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  Domestic exporters are required to sell most of their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings to commercial banks designated to trade on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The yuan's value is driven primarily by trade since it is fully convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to stay near 8.2770 - towards the firm end of its thin band - due to China's rosy trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  Average daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  turnover reached a record high of $394 million in the July to September quarter, 30 percent more than a year earlier, the official Xinhua News Agency said on Monday quoting the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 China Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Center. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the yuan sandwiched between 8.2760 and 8.2800, saying a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the key planks of its macroeconomic platform. \par \par \uc2  Officials have promised to widen the yuan's band gradually to cope with increasing flows of trade and foreign investment after China joined the World Trade Organisation in December, but have given no details or timetable. \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 6.6802 versus 100 yen after Friday's 6.6679 and softened against the euro to 8.1859 from 8.1597. It firmed a tick versus the Hong Kong dollar to 1.0607. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021014dyae00acn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
