\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Slightly Up On Exporter Dollar Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 06:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan was slightly higher against the dollar Monday as exporters sold the U.S. unit throughout the session to get rid of their large supplies of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the dollar was at CNY8.2767, down from CNY8.2769 Friday. \par \par \uc2  It was the fourth straight session the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen against the yuan, reflecting exporters' ample dollar supply due to China's strong export performance. \par \par \uc2  The pair fluctuated within a range of CNY8.2766 to CNY8.2770 during the session. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar sell orders dominated the trading for most of the session," said a trader at a local commercial bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  Late, heavy buying pushed the dollar up to CNY8.2767 towards the end of the session, however, and some players said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yuan for dollars. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the yuan's exchange rate in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  Most deals were conducted at the CNY8.2766 to the dollar level, the commercial bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  A car bombing in Indonesia Saturday that killed at least 188 people, which has caused some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to plunge, hasn't affected the yuan because of the tight controls on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate, traders said. \par \par \uc2  China strictly controls the flow of capital across its borders, allowing only partial convertibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the capital account. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on the current account is also tightly monitored and the value of the yuan is held in a narrow band against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Hong Kong dollar has declined to CNY1.0607 from CNY1.0608, the Japanese yen has climbed to CNY6.6802 per 100 yen from CNY6.6679, and the euro has strengthened to CNY8.1859 from CNY8.1597. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021014dyae0005t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
