\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Weaker Vs Dlr On Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2002\par 06:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan weakened against the U.S. dollar Monday on suspected selling by the People's Bank of China, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Large amounts of dollar buying pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above CNY8.2765, where it had settled the previous four sessions, to CNY8.2768 at 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. EDT Sunday). \par \par \uc2  "Ninety percent of today's trades were conducted at" CNY8.2767 to the dollar, where players think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, said a trader at a Chinese bank in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is doing this to bring liquidity to the market as the yuan has been at 8.2765 for four straight sessions," the trader added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the yuan's exchange rate in a tight band against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Monday's dollar/yuan trading range was typically narrow, only going from CNY8.2765 to CNY8.2768. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said they expect the yuan to strengthen again in coming sessions because exporters are loaded with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law they need to sell to banks, as China's trade surplus continues to be large. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be traded for current account purposes, and most exporters are required to sell 85% of their export receipts to state-owned banks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro weakened to CNY7.7123 from Friday's CNY7.7603, the Hong Kong dollar strengthened to CNY1.0606 from CNY1.0604, and the Japanese yen fell to CNY6.6568 per 100 yen from CNY6.7085. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020603dy630006a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
