\par\par \b \uc2  China c.bank says will expand yuan band gradually. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2002\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 9 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it will gradually ease the yuan's tight exchange rate band, provided it could be kept stable, to meet changes in trade and investment flows after joining the WTO. \par \par \uc2  The comment, from assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Li Ruogu, came just a week after U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill said the yuan's peg to the dollar could not be sustained for very long. \par \par \uc2  Li said there would be more changes in China's balance of payments following its entry into the World Trade Organisation in December and more factors would influence the exchange rate of the yuan, also known as the renminbi (RMB). \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to improve the current exchange rate regime, enhance coordination between the interest rate policy and the exchange rate policy, and appropriately expand the floating range of the RMB exchange rate provided that stability of RMB is maintained," Li said in a speech prepared for delivery on the sidelines of the Asian Development Bank's annual meeting. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the yuan trading in a narrow range of about 8.2760 to 8.2800 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not freely convertible on the capital account. \par \par \uc2  O'Neill said last week China would not be able to artificially keep the yuan peg for long by using its large dollar reserves. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think, however much their reserves might be, that they can get away very long with in effect defeating the market or producing a different relationship between their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world by using reserves to do it," O'Neill told the U.S. Senate Banking Committee on May 2. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $227.6 billion at the end of March, the second largest in the world behind Japan and boosted by a healthy trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  Li reinterated on Thursday China's oft-repeated pledges to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability while introducing more flexibility to absorb shocks to the gradually opening economy. \par \par \uc2  "In a country like China, whose economy is still in the early stage of development and the capital account remains under control, stability of exchange rates is beneficial to economic development," he said. \par \par \uc2  "In line with the domestic situation and the post WTO environment, we will push forward the process of RMB convertibility under capital account step by step." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020509dy5900e1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
