\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-U.S.'s O'Neill-China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  peg not sustainable. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anna Willard \par \uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 2002\par 19:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Adds background throughout) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, May 1 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill said on Wednesday that China will not be able to artificially keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged to a dollar range for long by using large U.S. dollar reserves. \par \par \uc2  China has been under pressure from the International Monetary Fund to gradually get rid of the yuan's virtual peg to the dollar and replace it with a peg to a more flexible basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Chinese authorities have said they are studying the proposal but have no plans to make changes in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "It's true that they're running what I would characterize as a semi-soft peg, but I don't think, however much their reserves might be, that they can get away very long with in effect defeating the market or producing a different relationship between their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world by using reserves to do it," O'Neill told the Senate Banking Committee. \par \par \uc2  "If it were true, then Argentina wouldn't be where it is today." \par \par \uc2  China's yuan currently trades in a narrow range of about 8.2760 to 8.2800 to the dollar, kept in check by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which uses \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within this range. \par \par \uc2  Last month, Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji said China had no plans to devalue the yuan or shift the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its virtual peg to the dollar to a peg to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon. \par \par \uc2  "Out of consideration for the interests of the region, and its own needs, China insisted on not devaluing its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We have continued to adhere to this policy, and this policy will not change," Zhu said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. MANUFACTURERS FEAR DEVALUATION \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the Japanese yen this year has sparked concern around the region that China might devalue the yuan, sparking a round of competitive devaluations by Southeast Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  U.S. manufacturers live in fear of a Chinese devaluation, as it could result in a flood of cheap Asian goods onto world markets undermining exports of U.S. products, which they say are already under pressure from U.S. dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  They argue that the yuan is already undervalued and would like the government to allow it to appreciate by refraining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  must abandon its mercantilist interference in exchange rate markets and allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate as market forces dictate," Thomas Palley, assistant director of public policy at the labor group AFL-CIO, said in a recent report. \par \par \uc2  In March, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Dai Xianglong said China was studying the IMF proposal to peg the yuan to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket of its major trade partners, but analysts said this was a long-term consideration and the yuan would remain stable for now. \par \par \uc2  China's top priority is to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as stable as it can during what promises to be a turbulent teething period in the World Trade Organization, and ahead of a top Chinese leadership reshuffle late this year, experts say. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020501dy5100upm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
