\par\par \b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Flat Vs Dlr, Yen At 3-Year Low Vs Yuan \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2001\par 05:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan finished unchanged at CNY8.2767 to the U.S. dollar Friday, while the yen fell to a three-year low versus the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell to CNY6.3901 per 100 yen Friday from Thursday's CNY6.4220, for its weakest close since Oct. 6, 1998 when it finished at CNY6.1850. \par \par \uc2  The yen/yuan decline comes as the yen plumbs fresh three-year lows against the U.S. dollar, in response to continued problems in Japan's stagnant economy. \par \par \uc2  "Since (\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yen/yuan trading, the yen's exchange rate always stays in close step with the international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a trader at Bank of America in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  "Some (exporters) are converting their excess yen receipts as soon as possible," he said. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted for foreign-trade purposes, and most exporters must repatriate 85% of their overseas receipts. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile Friday, the dollar traded between CNY8.2760 and CNY8.2769 before ending flat. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar fell slightly to CNY1.0606 from CNY1.0609. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011221dxcl0007a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
