\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan weakens on dollar bids by foreign banks. \b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2001\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened to end at a one-month low against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, partly due to increased dollar demand from foreign banks who began to close books for the year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar buying from local banks on behalf of importers also contributed to the fall in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at an intraday low of 8.2775 to the dollar, down from Tuesday's 8.2771 - the lowest close since October 29. It touched an intraday high of 8.2769. \par \par \uc2  Turnover figures were not available on Wednesday. Trade was moderate at $280 million on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign banks in China typically settle their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions late in the year so they can remit hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  profits to head offices before the end of the year. That helped push up dollar demand on Wednesday, they said. \par \par \uc2  "We have begun annual year-end settlement recently and the process will last for a few weeks," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said year-end settlement was likely to continue to exert some downward pressure on the yuan in the next few weeks, but they didn't expect a steep fall in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan was supported by China's healthy trade surplus, which was $17.33 billion from January to October. It would also be helped by increased shipments abroad ahead of the Christmas and New Year holidays, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to trade between 8.2770 and 8.2780 in the near term, closer to the strong end of its longstanding band of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  This would be slightly weaker than earlier this year, when the yuan regularly slipped outside the strong end of 8.2770. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  strictly enforced the tiny range through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for three years after the Asian financial crisis hit in 1997. But since April 2000 has allowed the yuan to close frequently, although only marginally, outside the band. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials have said the government planned to widen the yuan band gradually, but have offered no timetable. Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened to 6.7020 against 100 yen from Tuesday's 6.6585. It ended a notch firmer at 1.0612 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0613. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011128dxbs0066a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
