\par\par \b \uc2  China's yuan closes unchanged in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2001\par 06:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended flat against the U.S. dollar at 8.2771 on Tuesday due to a balance between dollar demand and sales by domestic banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said banks had seen roughly equal demand for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Chinese importers and sales of dollars by exporters. The yuan is convertible only on the current account and is mainly driven by trade flows. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed unchanged from Monday and moved in a tight range of 8.2769 and 8.2772 on sluggish turnover of $280 million versus Monday's $240 million. \par \par \uc2  A lack of fresh stimuli sidelined many bank traders who were reluctant to build new positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There was a rough balance of dollar supply and demand today, keeping the yuan in a narrow range," said a domestic bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has stayed strong for most of this year around 8.2770, the firm end of its longstanding thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800, as China reaped a trade surplus of $17.33 billion from January to October. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  strictly enforced the band through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for three years after the Asian financial crisis hit in 1997. But since April 2000 has allowed the yuan to close frequently, although only marginally, outside the range. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials have said the government planned to widen the yuan band gradually, but have offered no timetable. Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to hover around that level for the rest of the year as shipments abroad are typically higher ahead of the Christmas and New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  But they said the yuan might face some downward pressure next year as a slowing world economy bit into China's exports. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan strengthened to 6.6585 against 100 yen from Monday's 6.6641. It ended weaker at 1.0613 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0609. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011127dxbr00and\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
